  "interpretation": {
    "classification": "MANAGEMENT_TRADEOFF_DO_NOT_AUTOMATICALLY_ADVANCE",
    "rationale": [
      "Overall MAE improves numerically at both horizons and in all four chronological validation source seasons, but clustered 95% intervals for overall MAE cross zero at both Y2 and Y3.",
      "High-end underforecast bias improves clearly at >90th and >95th cohorts at both horizons; Y2 >95th MAE also has a clearly beneficial interval.",
      "Non-persistence and realized role-loss changes are small and their clustered intervals cross zero; no clear lower-tail harm is established.",
      "The strongest fitted effect is prior-two mean production level, especially at QB. The absolute-gap term is smaller and generally positive, so the evidence is stronger for multi-year level than for a simple 'stability is better' story.",
      "The directive's predeclared rule therefore maps this result to MANAGEMENT TRADEOFF, not automatic advancement."
    ],
    "next_action": "Return to management. Do not consume the final holdout. Any decision to carry this exact frozen candidate into the final exam requires a new explicit authorization."
